# .trivyignore — CVE / advisory suppressions for commercial-entitlements.
# Each entry must include an explanation and (where possible) an expiry date.
# Remove entries once the upstream fix is available and the image is re-pinned.
#
# Format: <CVE-or-advisory-ID> [exp:YYYY-MM-DD]
#         # comment explaining why it is suppressed and when to revisit

# DLA-4792-1: tzdata new timezone database (2026b → 2026c).
# This is a timezone data update, not a security vulnerability.
# gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot does not yet ship the fixed
# package version (tzdata 2026c-0+deb12u1); no patched distroless image is
# available upstream. Remove this entry once distroless ships tzdata 2026c.
DLA-4792-1

# DLA-4845-1: ca-certificates 20250419~deb12u1 → deb12u2 (removes the
# distrusted Comodo "AAA Certificate Services" and "emSign ECC Root CA - G3"
# roots). gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot does not yet ship the
# fixed package; the Dockerfile's pinned digest is already the latest
# upstream (checked 2026-11-22). The exposure itself is closed: the
# Dockerfile's certs stage (debian:bookworm-slim, deb12u2) replaces
# distroless's /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt — verified 150 → 148 certs,
# both roots absent. Trivy still reports the finding only because it reads
# distroless's dpkg status metadata. Remove this entry, the certs stage and
# its COPY, and bump the runtime digest once distroless ships deb12u2.
DLA-4845-1 exp:2026-12-22

# DLA-4854-1: tzdata 2026b-0+deb12u1 → 2026e-0+deb12u1, a timezone-database
# refresh (Trivy: UNKNOWN; the CI gate fails on UNKNOWN). Same package and
# situation as DLA-4792-1 above.
# Not exploitable here: the service never loads a zone (no time.LoadLocation,
# no time/tzdata, no time.Local use; all timestamps are UTC).
# Blocked upstream: distroless does not yet ship tzdata >= 2026e.
# Remove this entry and re-pin once distroless ships tzdata >= 2026e.
DLA-4854-1 exp:2026-11-30

# DLA-4867-1: tzdata 2026b-0+deb12u1 → 2026f-0+deb12u1, the next timezone-
# database refresh after DLA-4854-1 (Trivy: UNKNOWN; the CI gate fails on
# UNKNOWN). Same package and situation as DLA-4854-1 above.
# Not exploitable here: the service never loads a zone (no time.LoadLocation,
# no time/tzdata, no time.Local use; all timestamps are UTC).
# Blocked upstream: distroless does not yet ship tzdata >= 2026f.
# Remove this entry (with DLA-4854-1) and re-pin once distroless ships >= 2026f.
DLA-4867-1 exp:2026-11-30

# GO-2026-5932: golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp is unmaintained and unsafe by
# design (Trivy: UNKNOWN; the CI gate fails on UNKNOWN). Trivy flags the whole
# module (v0.58.0) in all three binaries.
# Not exploitable here: no package under cmd/, internal/ imports
# x/crypto/openpgp (go list -deps shows only sha3 and chacha20poly1305;
# the module arrives via testcontainers-go for x/crypto/ssh, test-only,
# not included in the production image). Remove this entry and bump
# x/crypto once a tagged release carries the fix.
GO-2026-5932 exp:2026-12-03
